{% extends "lab-base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Signal explorer · {{ data.target }}{% endblock %}
{% block scripts %}<script src="explorer.js" defer></script>{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<header class="lab-header explorer-header"><a class="back-link" href="investigations/archive.html">← The HIP544 investigation</a><p class="eyebrow">Signal explorer / Recorded telescope data</p><h1>A closer look<br><span class="title-muted">at every line.</span></h1><p class="lead">{{ data.rows|length }} classified rows, six scans, one bounded frequency window. Select a point or a table row to inspect its measurements and recorded checks.</p><div class="action-row"><a href="dossiers/{{ source.run_id }}.html" class="button-link">Evidence dossier →</a><a href="downloads/archive-hits.csv" class="button-link" download>Complete table · CSV ↓</a><a href="runs/{{ preparation.run_id }}/explorer.json" class="text-link" download>View data &amp; provenance</a></div></header>
<div class="callout-note warning-note"><strong>Historical results · original detector configuration.</strong><p>Later ON scans returned empty detector tables. {% if report %}A follow-up independently confirms below-threshold scores in those scans and recovers all 20 injected controls there. It also fixes a drift-coverage defect. <a href="research.html#first-report">Read the reproducible report →</a> {% endif %}These 273 rows remain the original clustered table. Survey completeness, the session census and external review are unfinished.</p></div>
<section class="section-block explorer-workbench" aria-labelledby="plot-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Find a line</p><h2 id="plot-title">The measured signal landscape</h2></div><p>Position shows frequency and drift. Colour shows the recorded classification. Select a point to inspect it; overlapping points can also be selected in the table.</p></div>
  <form class="explorer-controls" id="filters">
    <label>Classification<select id="verdict-filter"><option value="all">All classifications</option><option value="IN_OFF">In OFF scans</option><option value="SINGLE_POINTING">Single pointing</option></select></label>
    <label>Minimum SNR<input id="snr-filter" type="number" min="0" max="100000" value="0" step="1"></label>
    <label>Find a row<input id="hit-search" type="search" placeholder="ID or frequency" autocomplete="off"></label>
    <label>Order<select id="sort-order"><option value="snr">Strongest first</option><option value="frequency">Frequency</option><option value="drift">Drift</option></select></label>
    <button class="button-link" id="reset-filters" type="button">Reset</button>
  </form>
  <p class="figure-note" id="result-count" aria-live="polite">{{ data.rows|length }} of {{ data.rows|length }} rows · Recorded classifications</p>
  <div class="scatter-frame"><svg id="signal-scatter" viewBox="0 0 960 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="scatter-title scatter-description"><title id="scatter-title">Frequency versus drift for {{ data.rows|length }} measured rows</title><desc id="scatter-description">Cyan points occur in OFF scans; amber points are single-pointing rows. The full measurements are also available in the table below.</desc>
  {% for y, label in [(30,'+4'),(130,'0'),(230,'−4')] %}<line class="chart-grid" x1="65" y1="{{ y }}" x2="935" y2="{{ y }}"/><text class="chart-label" x="48" y="{{ y+4 }}" text-anchor="end">{{ label }}</text>{% endfor %}
  {% for x, label in [(65,'1380.0'),(239,'1380.2'),(413,'1380.4'),(587,'1380.6'),(761,'1380.8'),(935,'1381.0')] %}<line class="chart-grid" x1="{{ x }}" y1="30" x2="{{ x }}" y2="230"/><text class="chart-label" x="{{ x }}" y="252" text-anchor="middle">{{ label }}</text>{% endfor %}
  <text class="chart-label" x="500" y="280" text-anchor="middle">Recorded frequency · MHz</text><text class="chart-label" transform="translate(15 130) rotate(-90)" text-anchor="middle">Drift · Hz/s</text>
  <g id="scatter-points">{% for row in data.rows %}<a href="#row-{{ row.hit_id }}" data-hit="{{ row.hit_id }}" aria-label="Inspect {{ row.hit_id }}, {{ row.freq_mhz }} MHz, {{ row.verdict }}"><circle cx="{{ 65+(row.freq_mhz-1380)*870 }}" cy="{{ 130-row.drift_hz_s*25 }}" r="4" class="signal-point {{ 'point-off' if row.verdict == 'IN_OFF' else 'point-single' }}"><title>{{ row.freq_mhz }} MHz · {{ row.drift_hz_s }} Hz/s · SNR {{ row.snr }}</title></circle></a>{% endfor %}</g></svg></div>
  <div class="plot-key"><span><i class="key-off"></i>In OFF scans</span><span><i class="key-single"></i>Single pointing</span><span>Point size is constant; brightness does not encode significance.</span></div>
</section>
<section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="inspect-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / Follow the evidence</p><h2 id="inspect-title">A measurement, in context.</h2></div><p>Selection connects the scatter plot, the measured table and the recorded check notes. A vertical waterfall marker indicates the row's reference frequency, not a fitted trajectory.</p></div>
<div class="explorer-inspect">
  <aside class="selection-panel" id="selected-hit" aria-label="Selected measurement" tabindex="-1"><p class="eyebrow">Selected measurement</p><h3 id="selected-id">Choose a point or row</h3><p id="selected-verdict" class="selection-verdict"></p><dl id="selected-metrics" class="measurement-list"></dl><p id="selected-explanation"></p><div id="selected-checks" class="selected-checks"></div><p class="figure-note" id="selected-association"></p><a href="runs/{{ source.run_id }}/manifest.json" class="text-link">Original run record ↗</a><p id="selection-announcement" class="visually-hidden" aria-live="polite"></p></aside>
  <div class="waterfall-workbench"><div class="waterfall-heading"><h3>Six measured scans</h3><span class="tag">{{ data.scans|length }} archive previews</span></div>
  {% if data.scans %}
  <div class="waterfall-controls"><label>Frequency window<select id="zoom-window"><option value="1">Full 1 MHz</option><option value="0.25">250 kHz</option><option value="0.05">50 kHz</option></select></label><label>Centre · MHz<input type="range" id="frequency-centre" min="1380" max="1381" step="0.001" value="1380.5"><output id="frequency-readout" for="frequency-centre">1380.500</output></label><label>Display contrast<select id="contrast"><option value="2">−1 to +2 dB</option><option value="6">−1 to +6 dB</option><option value="12">−1 to +12 dB</option></select></label></div>
  <div class="waterfall-axis"><span id="frequency-left">1380.000</span><span>Frequency · MHz →</span><span id="frequency-right">1381.000</span></div>
  {% for scan in data.scans %}<div class="waterfall-scan"><div class="scan-label"><strong>{{ loop.index }} / {{ 'ON' if scan.role == 'A' else 'OFF' }}</strong><span>{{ scan.source }}</span><small>0 → {{ '%.1f'|format(scan.tsamp_seconds*scan.integrations) }} s ↓</small></div><canvas class="measured-waterfall" data-scan="{{ loop.index0 }}" width="1024" height="112" aria-label="Measured scan {{ loop.index }} of {{ scan.source }}; elapsed time increases downward. Preview requires JavaScript."></canvas></div>{% endfor %}
  <div class="colour-key"><span>−1 dB</span><span class="colour-ramp" aria-hidden="true"></span><span id="contrast-high">+2 dB</span></div>
  <p class="figure-note">{{ data.waterfall_method }} Native channels are averaged to roughly 1 kHz display bins; zoom does not restore native resolution. Time is relative to each scan start; gaps between scans are not shown.</p>
  <p class="figure-note">New preview processing: {{ preparation.finished_at.strftime('%d %b %Y') }} · <a href="runs/{{ preparation.run_id }}/manifest.json">Processing provenance</a></p>
  {% else %}<p>Waterfall previews are not available in this evidence package. The complete measured table remains inspectable.</p>{% endif %}
  <noscript><p class="callout-note">Interactive selection and waterfall previews require JavaScript. All {{ data.rows|length }} rows, the original plots in the dossiers, and the complete data downloads remain available.</p></noscript>
  </div>
</div></section>
<section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="table-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / Inspect every row</p><h2 id="table-title">The complete measured table</h2></div><p>ON and OFF counts are numbers of matching scans, not intensity or independent confirmations. Classified rows are not globally unique transmitters.</p></div>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="hit-table"><caption>All {{ data.rows|length }} rows from the source Parquet table. Use the controls above to filter.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Row</th><th scope="col">Frequency · MHz</th><th scope="col">Drift · Hz/s</th><th scope="col">SNR</th><th scope="col">ON / OFF</th><th scope="col">Classification</th></tr></thead><tbody id="hit-rows">{% for row in data.rows %}<tr id="row-{{ row.hit_id }}" data-hit="{{ row.hit_id }}"><th scope="row"><button type="button" class="row-select" data-hit="{{ row.hit_id }}" aria-label="Inspect {{ row.hit_id }}">{{ row.hit_id.split('-')[-1] }}</button></th><td>{{ '%.6f'|format(row.freq_mhz) }}</td><td>{{ '%+.6f'|format(row.drift_hz_s) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(row.snr) }}</td><td>{{ row.on_count }} / {{ row.off_count }}</td><td><span class="table-verdict {{ 'off' if row.verdict == 'IN_OFF' else 'single' }}">{{ 'In OFF scans' if row.verdict == 'IN_OFF' else 'Single pointing' }}</span></td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table><p class="empty-results" id="empty-results" hidden>No rows match these filters. Lower the minimum SNR or reset the filters.</p></div>
</section>
<script id="explorer-data" type="application/json">{{ data|tojson }}</script>
{% endblock %}
